        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>On the Logos prologue, Cyril resists any temporal reading of &#x27;in the beginning was the Word&#x27;: the Word is co-eternal with the Father, not produced as the first effect of the Father&#x27;s will. Cyril&#x27;s Miaphysite formula — &#x27;one nature of the incarnate Word&#x27; — anchors the Tewahedo christological tradition; the Ethiopian Liturgy of St Cyril (&#x27;Anaphora of Cyril of Alexandria&#x27;) is one of the principal eucharistic prayers of the Ethiopian Church to this day.</p></aside>',
