        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>&#x27;The true Light, which lighteth every man, was coming into the world&#x27; Cyril reads against the Manichaean and gnostic readings of his day: the Word&#x27;s illumination is universal, not restricted to a spiritual elite. Every rational creature receives some measure of the Word&#x27;s light — this is what makes humanity capable of recognizing Christ when He comes in the flesh. Cyril notes the imperfect tense &#x27;was coming&#x27; (erchomenon) as anticipating the Incarnation: the eternal illumination has always been preparing humanity for the historical advent of the Word made flesh.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk I.9 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
