        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>On &#x27;This beginning of miracles did Jesus&#x27; Cyril notes the programmatic placement: a wedding-feast miracle inaugurates the public ministry, signaling that Christ&#x27;s mission is nuptial in character — He has come to wed humanity to divinity in His own flesh. &#x27;Manifested forth His glory&#x27; (ephanerōsen tēn doxan autou) Cyril reads as the proleptic revelation of the cross&#x27;s glory: the Cana glory and the Calvary glory are one glory, the glory of the eternal Word visible in His incarnate works. The disciples&#x27; belief that follows is the first-fruits of the entire Church&#x27;s faith.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk II.11 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
