        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>AENON</strong> springs, a place near Salim where John baptized (John 3:23). It was probably near the upper source of the Wady Far’ah, an open valley extending from Mount Ebal to the Jordan. It is full of springs. A place has been found called ‘Ainun, four miles north of the springs.",
