    (
        4,
        23,
        "g",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>&#x27;The hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth&#x27; Cyril reads as the abrogation of the geographic-cultic restriction (Jerusalem temple / Mt. Gerizim) in favor of pneumatic-Christological worship. &#x27;In spirit&#x27; is for Cyril &#x27;in the Holy Spirit&#x27; (the worshipper&#x27;s pneumatic transformation), and &#x27;in truth&#x27; is &#x27;in the Truth that is Christ&#x27; (Jn 14:6). True worship after the Incarnation is therefore Trinitarian: to the Father, in the Spirit, through the Truth-Son. This passage grounds the Tewahedo liturgical doctrine that the Anaphora&#x27;s prayer is itself the Spirit&#x27;s praying through the Church to the Father, mediated by the Christological elements.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk II.23 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
    ),
