        "d",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Athanasius of Alexandria",
        "Athanasius of Alexandria (350).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Athanasius of Alexandria</strong> <em>Orationes contra Arianos III.16</em> <small>(c. 350 AD)</small><p>&#x27;That all men should honour the Son, even as they honour the Father. He that honoureth not the Son honoureth not the Father which hath sent him&#x27; — Athanasius marks hina pantes timōsi ton Huion kathōs timōsi ton Patera (that all should honor the Son EVEN AS they honor the Father) as the HOMOTĪMION (equal-honor) prooftext. Equal-honor is owed-by-creatures only to one equal-in-nature (homoousios) with the Father; therefore the kathōs (EVEN AS, in-the-same-manner-as) directly entails homoousion. Any reduction of the Son to creature-status would make this equal-honor idolatrous; the Word&#x27;s-own-claim therefore-positively-requires divine-essence. Pairs with Phil 2:10 (every-knee-shall-bow at-the-name-of-Jesus) as the canonical equal-divine-worship pair.</p></aside>',
        "Athanasius of Alexandria, Orationes contra Arianos (Four Discourses Against the Arians, I-IV), in Select Writings and Letters of Athanasius, Nicene and Post-Nicene Fathers (NPNF), Series 2, Vol. 4, ed. Archibald Robertson (Oxford / T&T Clark, 1892). PD. Greek text in Migne PG 26 (1857).",
