    (
        6,
        11,
        "a",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>On the multiplication of loaves Cyril notes the deliberate eucharistic prefiguration: Christ TOOK the loaves, gave THANKS (eucharistēsas), and distributed. The four-fold pattern (take / bless / break / give) that becomes the Mass Cyril sees inaugurated here — the feeding of the five thousand is the sign that points to the institution at the Last Supper and the perpetual continuation in the Anaphora. The crowd&#x27;s hunger Cyril takes typologically: humanity hungers for the bread of eternal life which only Christ can give; physical hunger is the symptom of the deeper spiritual hunger. The Tewahedo Anaphora&#x27;s preparation prayers preserve this typological reading explicitly.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk III.11 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
    ),
