    (
        7,
        39,
        "d",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>John&#x27;s interpretive aside — &#x27;This spake He of the Spirit, which they that believe on Him should receive: for the Holy Ghost was not yet given; because that Jesus was not yet glorified&#x27; — Cyril takes as decisive for the post-Pentecost-character of the Spirit&#x27;s full gift. &#x27;Was not yet&#x27; (oupō ēn) does NOT mean the Spirit did not exist (Cyril rejects this Origenist misreading) but that the Spirit had not yet been GIVEN in the new-covenant fullness — that giving awaits the Cross-Resurrection-Ascension sequence (&#x27;glorified&#x27; here meaning the entire paschal exaltation, not merely Resurrection appearance). After Pentecost the Spirit indwells the Church permanently as in 7:38; before Pentecost the Spirit comes intermittently as in the Old Testament prophets. This verse anchors Cyril&#x27;s pneumatology of progressive economy.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk V.39 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
    ),
