        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (428).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on the Gospel of John</em> <small>(c. 428 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And ye also shall bear witness, because ye have been with me from the beginning&#x27; Cyril takes as the apostolic-foundation text grounding the historical-witness character of the Christian message. &#x27;From the beginning&#x27; (ap&#x27; archēs) Cyril reads as the public-ministry beginning (from the Baptist&#x27;s witness onward) — the apostles&#x27; qualification to bear witness rests on direct historical eyewitness, not on personal religious experience alone. This grounds the patristic-Tewahedo doctrine of apostolic succession: the Church&#x27;s authoritative teaching traces back through a continuous chain to the eyewitness apostles, who saw with their own eyes what they then proclaimed.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on John, Bk X.27 (NPNF S2 V14). PD.",
