        "dict-easton",
        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>MALCHUS</strong> reigning, the personal servant or slave of the high priest Caiaphas. He is mentioned only by John. Peter cut off his right ear in the garden of Gethsemane (John 18:10). But our Lord cured it with a touch (Matthew 26:51; Mark 14:47; Luke 22:51). This was the last miracle of bodily cure wrought by our Lord. It is not mentioned by John.",
